/*
 * LVGL v9 UI layer implementation. See ui.h.
 *
 * M3 established the esp_lvgl_port glue — tick, task, mutex, flush, plus
 * panel-IO trans-done wiring — over the CO5300 panel and CST9217 touch
 * controller. UI-shell P1/P2 added the embedded fonts and color tokens
 * (ui_theme) plus the static orrery/star background on lv_layer_bottom() with
 * corner masks on lv_layer_top() (ui_background).
 *
 * UI-shell P3, this file's job at the time: replace the M3/M4 demo sampler
 * with the menu-first navigation shell — Home to submenu to action screens,
 * a screen stack with a 240ms directional slide (ui_nav), transparent screen
 * roots so the orrery shows through. P3.1 was the nav skeleton (Home, WiFi
 * submenu, the USB action screen carrying the existing M4 controls), meant
 * to prove the transparent-screen slide over the persistent orrery. Icons and
 * the larger type scale arrived in P3.2; the rest of the screen map (NFC/BLE/
 * System submenus, the WiFi Scan action shell) landed in P3.3.
 *
 * Load-bearing M3 invariants, kept verbatim (see the flush config below):
 *   - buffer_size is in pixels (the port multiplies by 3 for RGB888);
 *     .color_format = RGB888 (it defaults to RGB565); .buff_dma = false
 *     (the port rejects DMA buffers under RGB888).
 *   - the 2px ui_rounder_cb, since the CO5300 needs even column/row
 *     alignment or partial flushes come out sheared.
 *   - CONFIG_LV_COLOR_DEPTH_24=y (must literally be =y, not =24, or it's
 *     silently ignored).
 *
 * The P3.1 render-mode change fixed a banded, choppy nav slide by switching
 * from partial internal draw buffers to full-frame PSRAM buffers with
 * .full_refresh. Every frame now renders whole into a 410x502 PSRAM buffer
 * and flushes as one draw_bitmap call (the SPI bus's max_transfer_sz already
 * chunks it, per the M1 precedent) instead of being assembled band by band —
 * so a full-screen slide composes atomically rather than sweeping top to
 * bottom per frame. buff_spiram is required, since two full frames (1.23 MB)
 * won't fit in internal RAM but roughly 7.6 MB of PSRAM is free, and it frees
 * about 98 KB of internal RAM. full_refresh only renders and flushes when
 * something is actually invalidated, so an idle Home screen still never
 * repaints (preserving the P2 property); a periodic widget like the P4 clock
 * costs one full flush per tick.
 */
